      "math_academy_id": "q-101749",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Find the average rate of change of the function $y=-5x$ over the interval $x\\in [-1,-1+h]$, where $h>0$ is a parameter.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=-5x.$ Notice that we are given the length $h$ of the interval, so we use\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δy}{Δx}=\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h},\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1.$ Substituting into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5(-1+h)-(-5)(-1)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-5h-5}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5h}{h} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
